# Kotlin Gray-Part — Pitfalls & Fixes

Every entry below is a bug that actually occurred while building this app, with
the root cause and the fix. Apply these preventively in new projects.

---

## 1. `.debug` applicationIdSuffix breaks AppsFlyer attribution (CRITICAL)

**Symptom:** App always falls into native/white mode. Backend returns
`404 {"ok":false,"message":"No data"}`. AppsFlyer GCD returns
`400 {"error_reason":"App ID is incorrect"}`. Attribution body is empty.

**Cause:** `debug { applicationIdSuffix = ".debug" }` makes the package
`com.x.app.debug`. AppsFlyer/OneLink and Firebase are registered for the real
`com.x.app`, so attribution never binds.

**Fix:** Do NOT use `applicationIdSuffix` for debug. Keep the production
`applicationId` so AppsFlyer recognizes the install. Use only
`versionNameSuffix = "-debug"` if you need to distinguish builds.

```kotlin
buildTypes {
    debug { versionNameSuffix = "-debug" } // no applicationIdSuffix
}
```

Also keep `google-services.json` with the single real package (no `.debug`
client entry needed once the suffix is gone).

