## 7. AppsFlyer listener registered too late (no attribution)

**Symptom:** Attribution callback never fires; `awaitAttribution` times out.

**Cause:** passing `null` to `init()` then calling
`registerConversionListener` after `start()`.

**Fix:** pass the listener INTO `init`, then `start`. Bridge to coroutine:

```kotlin
private val attribution = CompletableDeferred<Map<String, Any?>>()
fun init() {
    val l = object : AppsFlyerConversionListener {
        override fun onConversionDataSuccess(d: MutableMap<String, Any?>) {
            CoroutineScope(Dispatchers.IO).launch {
                val data = if ((d["af_status"]?.toString())
                        .equals("Organic", true)) {
                    delay(5_000); fetchGcd() ?: d        // false-organic fix
                } else d
                if (!attribution.isCompleted) attribution.complete(data)
            }
        }
        override fun onConversionDataFail(e: String) {
            if (!attribution.isCompleted) attribution.complete(emptyMap())
        }
        override fun onAppOpenAttribution(p: MutableMap<String,String>?) {}
        override fun onAttributionFailure(p: String?) {
            if (!attribution.isCompleted) attribution.complete(emptyMap())
        }
    }
    AppsFlyerLib.getInstance().apply { init(key, l, ctx); start(ctx) }
}
suspend fun awaitAttribution(ms: Long) =
    withTimeoutOrNull(ms) { attribution.await() } ?: emptyMap()
```

